Changes made in this conversion (Swift Open License v1.0, Section 4(b)):

Source: ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4, revision
3ff0520224f264a2d0ac4ab56ece8f2f13aadb38 (UkisAI's ModelOpt NVFP4 quantization of
Swift 1.5 Qwen3.8-Flash-Next).

  - All model files (*.safetensors, config, tokenizer, chat template, generation and
    processor configs) were converted into one Infernix v3 artifact, stored as the
    three files Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-Dense8-Infernix-0000N-of-00003.infernix,
    with Infernix's tools.convert recipe qwen3_8_flash_next_nvfp4_dense8.
  - Routed experts: NVFP4 codes and scales copied unchanged, repacked into Infernix's
    expert layout.
  - Dense projections (GDN, QSA output, shared experts, hyper-connection mixers, PLE
    key/value projections) and lm_head: re-quantized from BF16 to 8-bit integers with
    one FP16 scale per 32 weights (q8_g32_fp16).
  - MTP drafter: re-quantized from BF16 (projections q8_g32_fp16, routed experts
    q4_g64_fp16).
  - Added a proposal head: q4_g64_fp16 copies of 131,072 lm_head rows.
  - PLE n-gram table: not included; the artifact binds to a separately distributed FP8
    n-gram volume, verified equal row for row to this model's table quantized to FP8.
  - GDN A_log and dt_bias widened from BF16 to FP32; other tensors kept as stored.
  - tokenizer.json: pre-tokenizer split pattern rewritten to the standard Qwen pattern;
    tokenizer_config.json: added_tokens_decoder built and prefix settings normalized.
  - README.md replaced; NGRAM-VOLUME.md and the conversion report added.
